      "limitations": [
        "the two substantive streams each pay their own coder header, and a noisy valuation stream adds entropy the single-stream coders do not pay at all; that is why the split is domain-specific",
        "on dithered or natural 24-bit material most valuations are effectively random and the split loses to a plain magnitude coder rather than beating one"
      ],
      "method": {
